Z||000005||Leadfoot||08-09-2001||01:14 PM||||The sticker is called the emissions label and someone suggested that we have a printable copy of it in the cave.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-09-2001||08:27 PM||||The VECI (Emmisions) labels are car specific. To be correct you'd need the one for your year/motor. They aren't serialized but they are dated. <P>I beleive the vin sticker he's talking about above are the ones that appear all over the car for the 87 model year on up. These labels are a U.S. Fed thing. You can get in trouble for removing/defacing them. That's why he's trying to mask them during repaint. They also help ID the car if it's stollen. Police know to look all over for these labels. If they can't find any or they are mismatched then they get real antsy about things.||||reg||1
